  "limitations": [
    "This is not a backtest. No trade is entered or resolved. No P&L, expectancy, win rate, drawdown, Sharpe, or profitability figure exists in this stage.",
    "The cost model is a Binance spot proxy. 26 bp round trip is not a measured Nobitex cost. A Nobitex deployment would need its own fee, spread, slippage, and fill measurements. The entry is the next 5m bar open; a gap between the confirmation close and that open is reflected in the stop distance but is not separately modelled as slippage.",
    "The definition is one instantiation of Stage 2B. The 1h/4h choice and the 72-bar/15% guards are engineering decisions made before counting. A different defensible instantiation could produce a different count; this census does not search for a more attractive one.",
    "The 2021-2024 window is one market regime mix. The 2022 bear market contributes relatively few signals. The result is conditional on this window.",
    "The non-overlapping count is a design count, not a tradable count. It assumes a 120h maximum holding horizon and ignores the actual exit path. It does not model stops, targets, or funding.",
    "Effective sample size is not identified. The Kish/cluster diagnostics are bounds and design heuristics; an outcome-based dependence estimate is not available at this stage.",
    "The control is not promoted. Its higher frequency is evidence about the regime filter's selectivity, not evidence that the unconditioned strategy is profitable.",
    "2024 is a partial year. The development interval ends 2024-07-01, so the 2024 row covers January-June only.",
    "Wide stops can be misleading. A 13% stop produces a low cost_R but a large position and large adverse exposure. The cost gate alone is not a risk judgement."
  ],
